## Scope Contract 3: Type Safety - Complete TypeScript Coverage

**Goal**: Replace all `any` types with proper Sanity TypeGen-derived interfaces

### Current State
```typescript
// catalogue-nav.types.ts
export interface CatalogueNavItem {
  id: string;
  label: string;
  imageUrl: string;
  sections: { title: string; links: string[] }[]; // ❌ links are just strings!
  feature: { caption: string };
}

// getCatalogueData.ts
function transformSanityToLegacyJson(items: CatalogueItem[]): { catalogue: any[] } // ❌ any[]!
```
- Navigation data uses `any[]` types
- No compile-time guarantees for catalogue structure
- Runtime errors possible if data shape changes

### Target State
```typescript
import type { CatalogueTreeNode } from "@/data/catalogue";
import type { SanityValues } from "@/sanity.types";

// Fully typed navigation items derived from Sanity schema
interface NavItem {
  id: string;
  label: string;
  url: string;
  sections: NavSection[];
}
```
- All catalogue structures use Sanity TypeGen types
- Compile-time validation for all data transformations
- IntelliSense support throughout navigation components

### Implementation
1. **Update `data/catalogue.ts` types**:
   - Use `CatalogueItem` from `sanity.types.ts`
   - Define strict interfaces for navigation transformation output
   - Export types for component consumption

2. **Update Navigation Components**:
   - Type `CatalogueNavbar`, `CatalogueView`, `NavbarManager` props
   - Remove all `any` types from catalogue-related files
   - Add type guards where necessary

3. **Verify Type Safety**:
   - Run `tsc --noEmit` with strict mode
   - Ensure zero type errors in catalogue system
   - Add type tests if needed

### DoD - Verification Checklist
- [ ] Zero `any` types in `data/catalogue.ts`
- [ ] Zero `any` types in `app/components/layout/catalogue/*`
- [ ] `tsc --noEmit` passes without errors
- [ ] All navigation props have explicit interfaces
- [ ] Link transformation includes proper URL types

### Testing
```bash
# Type checking
npx tsc --noEmit --project tsconfig.json

# Find remaining 'any' types in catalogue system
grep -r "any" app/components/layout/catalogue/ data/catalogue.ts || echo "No 'any' types found"
```

