## Notes & Risks

### Risk: Breaking Navigation Visual Behavior
**Mitigation**: Extensive visual regression testing before/after client component refactor. Maintain CSS class names.

### Risk: URL Path Mismatch with Existing Routes
**Mitigation**: Verify all 20 leaf slugs match `[...category]` route handler expectations. Test matrix of all category paths.

### Risk: Mobile Drawer Regression
**Mitigation**: `DrawersManager` keeps nuqs integration. Only inner content becomes server-rendered.

### Out of Scope
- **Product catalogueLocationKeys population**: Assumes products already have VFS keys assigned
- **Build script modifications**: Already complete per VFS_DATA_INTEGRITY_SPRINT
- **Category page redesign**: URL resolution only, no UI changes
- **New navigation features**: Feature parity only

---

## Sprint Completion Criteria

This sprint is complete when:
1. All 5 scope contracts pass DoD verification
2. Navigation renders with zero Sanity API calls
3. All 20 category links navigate to correct URLs
4. TypeScript coverage at 100% for catalogue system
5. Bundle size reduced by navigation client JS elimination
6. No visual or functional regressions in mega-menu/drawer

